From 8c8aae026c53860908672c6c291c16ff62e5b7a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite-Emulator Dev <dev@auralite-emu.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:25:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S5 update

STORE S5: large transfers + hardening.

All measured against the trees (frozen AuraLite-OS@0ed0d29):

- 128-KiB transfers: the engine already walked PRDTs of any size; the
  gap was the guest's own bounce ceiling (measured 128-KiB per-port
  bounce in AuraLite-OS drivers/ahci/ahci.c). tests/test_ahci.c 18 -> 22
  vectors pin the full 256-sector READ/WRITE DMA EXT shape (two 64-KiB
  PRDTs, golden bytes, prdbc == 131072), and NEW
  tests/integration/test_ahci_large_read.sh mirrors the QEMU
  test_ahci_large_read.sh gate guest-side: 16 MiB payload (the
  QEMU-side MEASURED size a bounce leak cannot survive) on a pre-built
  FAT32 at LBA 64 behind 64 zero sectors, typed
  `run /apps/filesize /fat/payload.bin`, asserting
  `FILESIZE /fat/payload.bin 16777216`, no reformat, no leak-ceiling
  truncation, byte-identical on re-run.

- --sata-writethrough: opt-in host write-through -- every guest WRITE
  DMA EXT byte also lands in the host image file at the same offset
  (ahci_wt_attach/ahci_wt_close_all). Default policy stays
  copy-on-attach in-memory; NEW
  tests/integration/test_ahci_writethrough.sh proves both policies with
  the same typed token: host byte-pristine without the flag, host image
  carries the token with it.

- Honest INTx: the AHCI 1.3 interrupt condition ((PxIS & PxIE) on any
  port, or HBA IS nonzero with GHC.IE) drives board line AHCI_IRQ0+ctrl
  (14/15, legacy IDE pairing) through pic_set_irq() into the PIC and the
  I/O APIC fan-out (CHIPSET H7 board wire); HBA IS is a live per-port
  PxIS aggregation. The guest driver polls with PxIE=0 and never sets
  GHC.IE (measured), so no receipt can move; `ok intx line` pins the
  line lifecycle (quiet under the guest contract, assert on unmask, W1C
  drop, GHC.IE aggregate path, LTIM level-follow on deassert).

- Hardening: tests/integration/test_ahci_matrix.sh grows
  MATRIX_DETERMINISM=1 (lanes A, B, C and the unattached lane E re-run
  sequentially, byte-identical -- measured x2 on the full matrix); the
  unattached negative-control lane is byte-identical on re-run and
  prints the unattached receipt verbatim.

Docs synced in this patch (ROADMAP store row CLOSED, STORE_PLAN S5
receipts, STATUS evidence, CHANGELOG incl. S1-S3 backfill).
